title: MeetingNiko
---
<<declare $playerName = "Holder">>
<<gatherVars>>

When you entered the library, the smell of new books and warm coffee washed
over you. The murmurs of students studying filled the room. The library was
always cozy, a place you liked to study and read assigned books.

A good candidate for this essay would definitely be here, you thought.
Bookworms could have the best opinions on life. You looked around for the
right person to ask.

You: "This is impossible,"

You sighed. Everyone was in groups, studying or chatting. You felt too awkward
approaching a group to ask about your questionnaire.

Turning to a bookcase, you shrugged and scanned the shelves. Nothing caught
your interest, and that's when you turned your head.

To your right stood a lone man dressed in blacks and browns, like a character
from a gothic novel. The only bright features were the blonde highlights in
his hair and his amber eyes as they scanned the books.

His hands brushed the spines delicately before stopping and selecting one
with precision. He opened it one-handed and read a few pages before nodding.

Then he turned, meeting your gaze with piercing eyes.

Startled, you quickly looked away, your face warming with embarrassment. You
heard him sigh.

<<setBool NikoDiaImageState true>>
Niko: "Do you need something?"
<<setBool NikoDiaImageState false>>

His voice was gravelly and rough, laced with annoyance. You didn't want to
bother him, but you needed a candidate. Maybe approaching a group would have
been easier.

-> walk away
    <<incRelationship "Niko" 1>>
    <<jump WalkAway>>
-> freeze up
    <<jump FreezeUp>>
-> walk towards him
    <<decRelationship "Niko" 1>>
    <<jump WalkTowardsHim>>
===

title: WalkAway
---
You decide you can't do it and quickly try to leave. You don't notice the pile
of books on the floor and trip.

You hit the ground with a loud thud.

Embarrassed, you scramble up, trying to escape.

<<setBool NikoDiaImageState true>>
Niko: "That looked like it hurt,"
<<setBool NikoDiaImageState false>>

He laughs mockingly, making your face burn. You've never felt more humiliated.

He watches you with a wide smile, clearly amused.

Swallowing your pride, you approach him anyway. His eyebrow raises at your
boldness.

You: "Hi, my name is {$playerName}. I need volunteers for my last essay in
Philosophy,"

You: "and I was wondering if you'd be interested in being one?"

You gather what confidence you can. He responds with an amused smile.

<<jump MeetingNiko2>>
===

title: FreezeUp
---
You: "Uhh..."

A terrible start. You sigh internally.

He looks down at you with quiet confidence, which irritates you. Still, you
push forward.

You: "Hi, my name is {$playerName}. I need volunteers for my last essay in
Philosophy,"

You: "and I was wondering if you'd be interested in being one,"

You explain your purpose as confidently as possible. He only raises an
eyebrow.

<<jump MeetingNiko2>>
===

title: WalkTowardsHim
---
You gather your confidence and approach him. He raises an eyebrow as you
near.

He turns fully to face you, towering over you. His eyes seem to glow under
the shadows, and he looks more annoyed than curious.

You begin to regret interrupting him.

You: "Hi, my name is {$playerName}. I need volunteers for my last essay in
Philosophy,"

You: "and I was wondering if you'd be interested in being one,"

You state your case. He responds with a soft scoff.

<<jump MeetingNiko2>>
===

title: MeetingNiko2
---
He looked at you with a bored expression, weighing his options as his hands
fiddled with the book. A sigh left his mouth as his gaze met yours again.

Niko: "Now why would I?"

You were stunned for a moment. You expected a simple yes or no, not a request
for justification. You blinked before straightening your posture to think of
a response.

-> Plead with him
    <<incRelationship "Niko" 1>>
    <<jump PleadWith>>
-> Reason with him
    <<jump ReasonWith>>
-> Argue with him
    <<decRelationship "Niko" 1>>
    <<jump ArgueWith>>
===

title: PleadWith
---
You felt hopeless at his condition. With little choice, you sighed and looked
up at him.

You: "Look, man, please just agree. I need candidates, and you're the only
person I approached without being scared. Please could you agree?"

He looked surprised, clearly not expecting you to beg. You felt pathetic and
embarrassed.

<<jump MeetingNiko3>>
===

title: ReasonWith
---
You began listing reasons.

You: "Well, first, the essay question is 'The end justifies the means.' Does
Niccolò Machiavelli's statement still apply to youth today? I feel like you'd
be a good candidate because-"

He pinched his nose and shushed you before you could finish.

<<jump MeetingNiko3>>
===

title: ArgueWith
---
You rolled your eyes, losing patience.

You: "What's your deal? You can't spare a few minutes to answer a question?"

Niko: "Excuse me?"

He looked at you in shock, shifting his weight as if ready to leave.

You: "Whatever, just decide already,"

This was a horrible idea.

<<jump MeetingNiko3>>
===

title: MeetingNiko3
---
He closes his eyes briefly, thinking, then sighs.

When he opens them, his expression softens.

<<setBool NikoDiaImageState true>>
Niko: "Okay,"
<<setBool NikoDiaImageState false>>

He sounds content.

<<setBool NikoDiaImageState true>>
Niko: "I agree to volunteer for your candidates,"
<<setBool NikoDiaImageState false>>

He seems more approachable now, his guard lowered. Whatever you said convinced
him.

He shifts and faces you fully. The tension around him fades.

You notice a satchel on his shoulder and the book he holds.

The book is gold-lined, titled "Wuthering Heights."

<<setBool NikoDiaImageState true>>
Niko: "My name is Niko. I'm studying Music. Nice to meet you,"
<<setBool NikoDiaImageState false>>

He extends his hand. You hesitate before shaking it.

His hand is cold, and he pulls away quickly, grimacing.

You: "It's nice to meet you too,"

You give him your first question. He looks confused, but after your
explanation, he nods slowly.

<<setBool NikoDiaImageState true>>
Niko: "I'll answer this tomorrow...goodbye for now,"
<<setBool NikoDiaImageState false>>

Just like that, he dismisses you and walks away.

You watch him go, unsure what to think.

-> Like him
    <<jump EndingPart>>
-> Don't mind him
    <<jump EndingPart>>
-> Don't like him
    <<jump EndingPart>>
===

title: EndingPart
---
You've got a candidate sorted. No need to stay any longer.

Time to head home...
===